.TH VDL 1 "2026-11-06" "vdl 2.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vdl \- portable smart downloader for Linux and Termux (yt-dlp + aria2c)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIurl\fR | \fIlinks.txt\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdl
is a Bash downloader that routes downloads intelligently: direct files
(archives, ISO images, PDFs, magnet links, \fI.torrent\fR files, plain video
files) are sent to
.B aria2c
when it is installed for parallel segmented downloads, while pages, playlists,
and streams are handled by
.B yt-dlp.
Either engine can be used alone with
.BR --no-aria .
.PP
When no URL is given on the command line,
.B vdl
attempts to read a link from the clipboard (wl-paste, xclip, or xsel).
.PP
All yt-dlp defaults are baked into
.B vdl
itself; it runs yt-dlp with
.B --ignore-config
so the user's global
.IR ~/.config/yt-dlp/config
is never touched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-browser " " \fINAME\fR
Browser to take cookies from (default: auto-detect).
Supported: vivaldi, firefox, brave, chromium, chrome, edge, opera, safari, whale, none.
A profile may be appended with \fB:\fR, e.g. \fBfirefox:work\fP.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no-cookies
Do not read browser cookies.
.TP
.B \-\-cookies \fIFILE\fR
Read cookies from a Netscape-format \fIcookies.txt\fP file.  Useful on
Termux and other systems where yt-dlp cannot read browser profiles directly.
.TP
.B \-\-root-cookies
Termux root only: copy Firefox for Android's cookie database out of
app-private storage with
.B su
and pass it to yt-dlp.  Chrome, Chromium, Brave, and other Android
Chromium-based browsers encrypt their cookie values with the Android
Keystore, so they are not supported by this option; export a cookies.txt
file instead.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " " \fIMAXHEIGHT\fR
Maximum video height (default: 1080; 2k=1440, 4k=2160).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audio
Audio only, converted to MP3 320k.
Output goes to \fIsave_dir\fR/audio.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-batch-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read URLs from FILE (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-download-dir \fIDIR\fR
Override
.IR VDL_SAVE_DIR
for this invocation.
.TP
.B \-\-no-aria
Do not use aria2c; direct files go to yt-dlp as well.
.TP
.B \-\-no-impersonate
Disable browser TLS impersonation.
.TP
.B \-\-referer \fIURL\fR
Send this Referer header.
.TP
.B \-\-user-agent \fIAU\fR
Send this User-Agent header.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy \fIURL\fR
Route downloads through this proxy.
.TP
.B \-\-aria-opts \fIOPTS\fR
Extra options forwarded to aria2c (e.g.
.I "\-\-max-connection-per-server=8").
.TP
.B \-\-max-speed \fIRATE\fR
Maximum overall download speed (aria2c) or rate cap (yt-dlp).
.TP
.B \-\-limit-speed \fIRATE\fR
Per-download speed limit.
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Save a single download under this filename (the extension is appended when
NAME has none).  For a playlist URL, NAME becomes the folder name instead.
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Exact destination for a single URL.  A PATH whose last component has an
extension is the exact file; otherwise PATH is the exact folder (playlist
items go directly inside it).  Cannot be combined with \-\-name.
.TP
.B \-\-zip\fR[\fB=\fINAME.zip\fR]
Archive this run's downloads into a zip in the save directory.  With no
name, an automatic vdl-<timestamp>.zip is used.  Requires the zip command.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the resolved plan (engine, mode, URLs, save dir) without downloading.
.TP
.B \-\-dedupe
After downloading, remove files from this run whose content is identical to
another file downloaded in the same run (the oldest copy is kept).
.TP
.B \-\-images
Also download images embedded in album pages (opt-in; see the user guide for
which pages are scanned).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress the banner, status lines, summary, and downloader progress output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.PP
Any option not recognised by
.B vdl
is passed straight through to yt-dlp.  Flags that take a value can always be
written as \fB\-\-flag=value
so that the form is never mistaken for a URL or a batch file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDL_SAVE_DIR
Download directory (default: XDG download dir +
.IR /vdl ;
on Termux, \fI~/storage/downloads/vdl\fP when storage is set up).
.TP
.B VDL_BROWSER
Default browser, overridden by
.BR \-b .
.TP
.B VDL_COOKIES
Netscape cookies.txt file passed to yt-dlp, overridden by
.BR \-\-cookies .
.TP
.B VDL_ROOT_COOKIES
Set to \fB1\fR or \fBfirefox\fR to import Firefox Android cookies via root
on Termux.
.TP
.B VDL_WAKELOCK
Set to \fB0\fR to disable the automatic Termux wake lock.
.TP
.B VDL_QUALITY
Default max height, overridden by
.BR \-q .
.TP
.B VDL_TMP_KEEP_DAYS
Days to keep interrupted leftovers (default: 7).
.TP
.B VDL_IMPERSONATE
\fBauto\fR (first available target yt-dlp reports), \fBoff\fR, or a target name.
.TP
.B VDL_CONFIG
Extra yt-dlp config file (default
.IR ~/.config/vdl/yt-dlp.conf ).
Loaded in addition to the defaults baked into
.BR vdl .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vdl/config
Optional vdl-specific config file.  A simple
.B KEY=VALUE
file; recognised keys mirror the
.B VDL_*
environment variables and are overridden by flags and exported environment
variables.
.TP
.I ~/.config/vdl/yt-dlp.conf
Extra yt-dlp options loaded via
.BR VDL_CONFIG .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
vdl                                    # URL from clipboard
vdl "https://example.com/video"
vdl links.txt                            # every URL listed in links.txt
vdl -q 720 links.txt
vdl -a "https://example.com/album"        # MP3 320k
vdl -n "https://example.com/file.iso"     # direct file, no cookies
vdl --cookies cookies.txt "https://example.com/video"  # manual cookies
vdl --root-cookies "https://example.com/video"  # Termux + root + Firefox
vdl --output ~/Videos/movie.mp4 "https://example.com/video"
vdl --zip=my-batch.zip links.txt
vdl --no-aria -F "https://example.com/video"  # list formats
vdl --dry-run "https://example.com/file.iso"   # preview routing
vdl --download-dir ~/tmp "https://example.com/file.zip"
vdl --aria-opts "--max-connection-per-server=8" "https://example.com/file.iso"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR aria2c (1),
.BR mktemp (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the project's GitHub issue tracker.
